Customer Retention & Churn Analysis
 Project Overview

This project focuses on analyzing customer behavior to understand why customers leave (churn) and how businesses can improve customer retention.
The analysis is performed using Power BI, with interactive dashboards and business insights.

 Objectives
Analyze customer churn patterns
Identify high-risk customer segments
Understand customer retention behavior
Provide actionable recommendations
🛠️ Tools Used
Microsoft Power BI – Dashboard & visualization
Microsoft Excel – Data preparation
CSV Dataset – Customer data
  Dataset Description

The dataset contains customer-related information such as:

Customer ID
Gender
Tenure (months)
Contract type
Payment method
Monthly charges
Churn status (Yes/No)
📊 Dashboard Features
Customer distribution analysis
Contract type vs churn
Payment method analysis
Tenure vs churn trends
Interactive filters (gender, contract)
🔍 Key Insights
Month-to-month customers have the highest churn rate
Customers with low tenure are more likely to leave
Long-term contracts improve customer retention
Electronic check users show higher churn
💡 Recommendations
Offer discounts for long-term subscription plans
Improve onboarding experience for new customers
Promote auto-payment methods
Identify and target high-risk customers early
📈 Project Output
Interactive Power BI dashboard
Business insights & recommendations
Data-driven decision support
